red{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T10:45:14Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T10:45:14Z","body":"@TokageItLab I think there's some confusion.  \n\nThe issue is not that 4.6 animations are not compatible with 4.7 if `deprecated=no`.\n\nThe problem is: new projects created with 4.7.dev cannot use blendspaces if Godot was built with `deprecated=no`.\n\nThis issue persists if the only version involved is 4.7.dev, configured with `deprecated=no`.\n\nMy past contributions have mostly been catching build errors that didn't fully account for `DISABLE_DEPRECATED`, is this build configuration going to be removed?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4074021380/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4074237759","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117490#issuecomment-4074237759","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117490","id":4074237759,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7y1-8_","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user